Aspirational: a handle-addressed store read (`pool[h].f`) lowers only inside a
write block. The declaration's whole-program pass rewrites SINGLETON cell paths
(`ui.sel`) and not indexed ones, so a guard or an interpolation reaches the host
verbatim. std/grid closed the same gap for cells on 2026-08-03; this is the
store half, and it is the second-lowering problem rather than a missing feature
— `indexedFieldRefs` already exists, in a helper struct the `new` walk cannot
see.
